IMPORT prelude

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06, from
-- the plain-text rendering uksi-2015-173.txt (not the official text).
--
-- LAYER 1, NOUNS: the records and choices that more than one module needs.
-- Nothing in this file is a rule and nothing is evaluated.
-- A "noun" here is a fact that a witness of ordinary competence could state without
-- reading the Regulations (when something happened, which manner was used, which
-- of two things was chosen).
-- Part-specific records are declared in the module of the Part that uses them, so
-- that no name is defined in two modules (the seat imports them all).

§ `Shared nouns`

-- How a person gives notice or makes a choice to the Secretary of State.
-- Regulations 5(2), 6(2)(d), 7(2) and 18(3) list the manners; "another manner"
-- stands for any manner they do not list.
DECLARE MannerOfNotice IS ONE OF
    `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State`
    `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State`
    `in another manner`

-- The two things a survivor may choose between (regulations 4 to 6 and 18 to 20):
-- a lump sum, or a state pension.
-- Regulations 4 to 6 speak of "a lump sum under section 8" and "a state pension
-- under section 9" of the 2014 Act; regulations 18 to 20 of "a lump sum under
-- regulation 19" and "a state pension under regulation 20".
DECLARE PaymentChoice IS ONE OF
    `a lump sum`
    `a state pension`

-- Both dates are days on which entitlement is deferred (first and last day).
-- src:20 | “deferral period” means the period during which a person’s entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred;
@ref Regulation 1(4), "deferral period" (src:20)
DECLARE DeferralPeriod HAS
    `first day of the deferral` IS A DATE
    `last day of the deferral` IS A DATE
